# What the daemon receives before the first instruction of the Dockerfile runs. Everything here is
# either build output the image is about to produce for itself, local runtime state, or the
# repository's paperwork.
#
# The first two patterns are the ones that matter: copying Windows-built bin/obj into a Linux build is
# how a stale obj/project.assets.json or a Debug assembly from the host ends up inside the image.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Host tooling and repository metadata.
.vs/
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.freebuff/

# Documents, never published and never needed to compile.
docs/
*.docx
*.md

# Local databases (the SQLite fallback writes these) and anything a run leaves behind.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
artifacts/

# Secrets, and the compose file itself: the images are built from, not with, these.
.env
*.env
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
